# release-content-guard.sh patterns — one glob per line, # comments and
# blank lines ignored. A path matching any pattern here is rejected from a
# commit (pre-commit --staged) or a push (pre-push --range) — content is never
# inspected, only the path. Extend this file per-repo; the guard itself never
# hard-codes a pattern of its own.

# Session memory — local only, read from disk by the SessionStart hook, never
# committed (references/progress-file.md).
PROGRESS.md

# A generated handoff snapshot (skills/handoff), timestamped by the skill that
# writes it — not the skill's own template, which is legitimately tracked.
**/handoff-[0-9]*.md

# A break-run.sh mutation marker left behind by a dead falsification run.
*.devkit-break

# Generated test output — produced by running the suite, never a static test
# source. A file under a testdata/ directory is a fixture, not output, and is
# never matched by these patterns. `**/` makes these depth-agnostic — a
# report nested under a module directory is still caught, not just one at the
# repo root; *.lcov, *.pyc and *.devkit-break already cross `/` on their own
# since the guard matches paths, not filenames.
**/coverage.out
*.lcov
**/coverage/**
**/junit*.xml
**/test-results/**
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/__pycache__/**
*.pyc
